description: Scroll and keyboard behavior for marketplace screens with inputs
globs: src/ui/**/*.tsx,src/pages/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Screen scroll and keyboard

Apply this on every screen that has text inputs, including each Maweja page.

- Hide the scroll indicator: `showsVerticalScrollIndicator={false}`.
- Put bottom spacing on `contentContainerStyle`, not on the ScrollView style. Include the safe area plus extra space so the last button can scroll fully into view.
- One vertical scroll per screen. An embedded form must not start a second ScrollView (`scrollEnabled={false}` when it sits inside a parent scroll).
- While the keyboard is open, the user must be able to scroll to the submit button and tap it without dismissing the keyboard first. Set `keyboardShouldPersistTaps="handled"`. On iOS, add the keyboard height to the content bottom padding (`useKeyboardInset`). Android already resizes the window.
- Do not leave the action button behind the keyboard.
- Maweja chrome uses `colors.primary`. Do not hardcode the red from the still. Validation errors stay `colors.danger`.

# Maweja listing

Match the stills. Keep the original layout when the design is not maweja.

- Top business cards are the compact ones: smaller width, shorter image, logo and name over the photo, time and delivery on one line under it.
- Store cards keep a border and inner padding. Fill the empty space with store data that already exists: type, time, delivery price, and distance. Separate those facts with a bar and keep that row inside the text block, under the store name and beside the logo, not as a full-width row under the logo. Show the same values and format as the original card: the fee goes through `parsePrice` even when it is zero, never a "free delivery" label.
- Categories are one horizontal line of pills. The selected pill uses the brand color. Do not stack them in a second row.
- Search, notifications, and the cart stay fixed above the list while it scrolls. Pickup and the map stay in the scrolling content. Do not change where those controls navigate.
- While list content passes under that bar, its background switches to `colors.primary`, including the status bar and notch. At the top of the list it returns to the page background.

# Maweja business menu

The business screen is two steps. Keep the original menu when the design is not maweja.

- First step: business hero, then a two-column grid of the categories the core already returns. No synthetic All or Featured tile.
- Second step: the selected category's products. The back control returns to the grid. The hero back leaves the business.
- Product rows keep the existing product action: options open the product screen, and one-click add stays behind its config.
- Do not add the chat button from the still, and do not change the tab bar.

# Maweja cart

Keep the original cart when the design is not maweja. There are two pages.

- The header cart button opens the cart list. Each row is one business cart: name, product count, total. The count on this page is carts, not products. Opening a row pushes that business cart.
- The business page opens only the cart for the store you are in. That page lists products, and its checkout button is the step into checkout.
- On the business cart, the header is the title, the product count, and the trash control. The delivery address is a card in the scroll. Checkout is full width and stays fixed at the bottom.
- Change on the address card opens `AddressList` (or `AddressForm` for a guest) with `isGoBack: true`. Picking, editing, or creating an address returns to this cart, never to Home. The list replaces itself with the form so one back lands on the cart.

# Maweja checkout

Keep the original checkout when the design is not maweja. The place-order path, payment forms, and validation stay.

- Articles is the product list: photo, name, quantity times price, line total.
- Recipient shows the saved customer values. Edit on the title opens the fields, and Close returns to those values.
- Delivery address is a card in the scroll, not the page header.
- There is no selected-method summary card. The method list is vertical cards. Wallets and loyalty points are not shown in the Maweja checkout.
- The card_delivery gateway is labeled Mobile Money. Its hint lists M-Pesa, Orange Money, Airtel Money, and IllicoCash.
- The invoice keeps the existing totals, adds the delivery zone when the cart has one, and shows the estimated time and the secure-payment note when those values exist.

# Maweja order details

Keep the current order details content. The Maweja pieces are added for the tracking stills and do not replace the existing header, products, addresses, comments, or payment rows.

- Tracking header, status pill, pending and delivered banners, delivery progress, driver map card, delivery agent title, and summary title.
- Confirmed and on-the-way banners, the third driver action, and pickup-specific steps are not in this pass. The existing blocks stay so those gaps stay visible.
